#     `if (!score_ids.empty()) return score(...)` right after the --serve dispatch (before --ppl / the CLI decode), with
#     window and std::atoi(eos) exactly as Strata passes them; usage() text gains the --score line; `#include <numeric>`
#     (std::iota; Strata's file includes it, Maya's did not).
#   Nothing else changes: the new code runs only when --score is given.
#
# API differences adapted / checked by reading (v1.1.28 vs v0.2.6):
#   - Error prefix: Strata's "strata-dsv41: ..." -> "maya-ds4: ..." (4 lines; error paths only, nothing parses them).
#   - --window default: Strata declares window = 0 and sets 16 before its scoring dispatch; Maya declares window = 16
